      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **Approved with minor suggestions** — See inline comments for optional improvements.\n\n### Review Summary\n*   **Functionality:** The fix correctly changes the array type to `struct usb_mux_chain` and nests the inner `struct usb_mux` via a compound literal to prevent the `memcpy` overflow.\n*   **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** The array declaration aligns with the current board configuration conventions and properly maps the types.\n*   **Code Simplicity:** The use of an anonymous compound literal for `.mux \u003d \u0026(const struct usb_mux) {...}` is clean and avoids polluting the file with single-use named structs.\n*   **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** The struct initialization is idiomatic C99 and clearly maintains the existing layout without unrelated changes.\n*   **Security:** No security issues introduced; fixing a buffer overflow improves memory safety.\n*   **Testing:** This fixes a hardware boot panic. I left a minor suggestion to add a `BUILD_ASSERT(sizeof(usb_muxes) \u003d\u003d sizeof(ampton_usb_muxes));` to enforce this layout constraint at compile time and prevent future regressions.\n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** Size: S (+21, -17). The CL is atomic and follows the Single Logical Change rule.\n*   **Commit Message:** The description accurately captures the issue and the fix, maintaining appropriate altitude and formatting.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/26f94729-13a2-49b7-9c9d-95ebaeca28da)",
